<section id="takeaways" class="takeaways"><h2>Key takeaways</h2><ul>
<li><strong>Start with one SOP.</strong> Pick a repeatable task with a clear trigger, owner, and outcome.</li>
<li><strong>Use rules for predictable steps.</strong> Use AI when a step needs to interpret emails, notes, or varied document formats.</li>
<li><strong>Give exceptions a home.</strong> Name the person who reviews uncertain cases, corrects errors, and approves consequential actions.</li>
<li><strong>Measure the workflow before rollout.</strong> Record manual minutes per case, turnaround time, and the rate of errors or rework.</li>
</ul></section>
<section id="definition"><h2>What does an AI automation agency do?</h2>
<p>An AI automation agency designs, builds, and integrates systems that complete repeatable business tasks. A workflow might read an incoming request, extract fields, check them against a CRM record, and send incomplete cases to an operations queue. The agency typically maps the process, connects the tools, tests real examples, and defines how staff handle exceptions.</p>
<p>A chatbot mainly answers questions in a conversation. A workflow can act across several systems, with access limited to the records and actions it needs. Many workflows combine both deterministic rules and AI interpretation.</p></section>
<section id="method"><h2>How to evaluate an AI automation agency</h2>
<p>Use the same four questions for every proposal. Ask the vendor to walk through one routine case and one exception using anonymized examples.</p>
<ul><li><strong>Workflow fit.</strong> Can the team map the trigger, inputs, rules, exceptions, and output using your SOP?</li>
<li><strong>Integration and approvals.</strong> Which tools will it access, what can it change, and which actions need a person to approve them?</li>
<li><strong>Success measures.</strong> Which metric will the pilot improve? Compare handling time at similar volumes while tracking error and rework rates.</li>
<li><strong>Ownership and support.</strong> Who owns the code and accounts? Ask who monitors failures, updates the workflow when an API changes, and documents the manual fallback.</li></ul>
