<section id="comparison"><h2>Rules-based automation vs. custom AI</h2><p>Choose the simplest approach that can handle the input and the cost of getting it wrong.</p>
<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Automation options"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Approach</th><th scope="col">Best for</th><th scope="col">Example</th><th scope="col">What to test</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th scope="row">Rules-based workflow</th><td>Structured inputs and known steps</td><td>Route form submissions by region</td><td>Missing fields and duplicate events</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">AI-assisted workflow</th><td>Text or documents that vary</td><td>Extract fields from emailed requests and queue uncertain cases</td><td>Field accuracy and review workload</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Custom AI integration</th><td>Multi-step processes spanning several systems</td><td>Prepare a review packet in an internal tool and log the reviewer’s decision</td><td>Access controls, retries, audit trail, and fallbacks</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div></section>
