<section id="faq"><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
<details open><summary>How do I choose an AI automation agency?</summary><p>Give each agency the same SOP and ask how it would handle normal cases, exceptions, system access, and human review. Compare what each vendor would measure and who would own the system after launch.</p></details>
<details><summary>Which workflow should I automate first?</summary><p>Choose a high-frequency task with a named owner, clear inputs, and a measurable output. CRM updates, document intake, and lead routing are good candidates when their exceptions are easy to identify and review.</p></details>
<details><summary>When are tools like Zapier or n8n enough?</summary><p>A workflow platform can be enough when triggers and actions are well-defined and your team can maintain them. Consider custom work when you need complex integrations, inconsistent inputs, or a tailored approval and audit process.</p></details>
<details><summary>How much does AI automation cost?</summary><p>Price depends on the number of workflows, their exceptions, the integrations involved, and the support needed. Vixera Labs says it provides a fixed quote after its free audit.</p></details>
<details><summary>How should I measure a pilot?</summary><p>Record a baseline before launch. Compare median handling time and error or rework rates at similar volumes, then check how many cases still require staff intervention.</p></details>
<p>Have an SOP in mind? <a href="mailto:harsh@vixeralabs.com?subject=Free%20AI%20automation%20audit">Book a free automation audit with Vixera Labs</a> to discuss where to start.</p></section>

